/**
 * @page scripts Python tools
 * Python packages for field data, validation, sweeps, plotting, placement
 * baselines and RL. Run each as `python -m scripts.<pkg>.<module>` from
 * `scratch/mesh-sim/`.
 *
 * ## Simulation tools
 * - @subpage scripts_arpo_data — Turns raw ARPO field-test CSVs into per-day plots, GPS traces and per-scenario traces
 * - @subpage scripts_validation — Checks simulator output against ARPO field data and against stored regression results
 * - @subpage scripts_sweep — Runs a grid of simulations from one sweep INI file into a single output folder
 * - @subpage scripts_plotting — Turns simulator CSV and JSON outputs into figures
 * - @subpage scripts_baselines — Plans geometric and optimization node placements before a run, scored by the simulator channel
 * - @subpage scripts_baselines_planners — The two placement planners, their shared objective and the channel scorer
 * ## RL tools
 * - @subpage scripts_rl — Command guide for RL training, evaluation, comparison and experiment matrices
	* - @subpage scripts_rl_env — Gymnasium environment that runs the simulator as a subprocess over the RL JSON protocol
	* - @subpage scripts_rl_agents — MaskablePPO wrapper, training callbacks and an exploratory Q-learning agent
	* - @subpage scripts_rl_ops — Benchmarking, tuning and cluster operations for an experiment plan
	* - @subpage scripts_rl_policy — Verifies a saved training run, runs policies and computes paired statistics
	* - @subpage scripts_rl_tests — Map of the RL, ops and placement-baseline Python tests and their helpers
	* - @subpage scripts_rl_experiments — Batch domain: matrix version 2 validation, the plan v3 task graph and named selection rules
	* - @ref mesh_sim_rl_batch_reference "Batch experiment reference" — Every batch field, path, identity, state, protocol and the retired-command map
 */

/**
 * @page src Simulator modules
 * C++ simulator source modules, split by concern. All code lives in namespace
 * `mesh_sim`.
 *
 * ## Simulation modules
 * - @subpage src_domain — Plain-struct configuration and result types shared by every simulator layer
 * - @subpage src_config — Loads `run.ini` and its JSON files into a `SimConfig` and checks it for errors
	* - @subpage src_config_run_ini_reference — Every `run.ini` key the simulator reads, with defaults and units
 * - @subpage src_eval — Computes radio link quality for every node pair each simulation tick
 * - @subpage src_routing — Flow-level routing over the mesh link graph, with congestion scaling and latency
 * - @subpage src_jammer — Adds interference from jammer emitters to per-link SINR in the sub-6 band
 * - @subpage src_traffic — Flow-level traffic demand generation
 * - @subpage src_io — Writes the output files: per-tick CSVs, a per-seed JSON summary, a run log and progress
 * - @subpage src_util — String, path and INI helpers shared by config, cli and io
 * - @subpage src_cli — Command-line parsing and pre-simulation setup
 * - @subpage src_setup — Creates the ns-3 nodes, mobility models, buildings and propagation models for a run
 * - @subpage src_query — `--channel-query`: scores candidate start layouts through the simulator's own channel path
 * ## RL modules
 * - @subpage src_rl — Wire contract for the stdin/stdout JSON bridge to the Python Gymnasium environment
	* - @subpage src_rl_policy_inputs — Observation presets, reward components and telemetry for centralized policies
	* - @subpage src_rl_policy_input_tests — Map of the centralized RL and policy-input tests
	* - @subpage src_rl_policy_lifecycle_tests — Map of the policy lifecycle (validate, train, inspect, evaluate) tests
	* - @subpage src_rl_policy_comparison_tests — Map of the policy comparison, experiment-matrix and evaluation-pipeline tests
	* - @subpage src_rl_decision_records — Opt-in per-episode records of what a centralized policy saw, requested and got back
 */
